  "description": "CR 709.5g locking each door takes both designations back away",
  "note": "Synthetic Skeleton Key's \"{T}: Lock each unlocked door of target Room\" is CR 709.5g in the plural: both designations come off in one activation and the Room has no name (CR 709.5). Rules 709.5h and 709.5i both ask about a permanent GAINING a designation, so nothing fires and neither Leech costs anyone a life, which would catch a lock routed through the unlock writer. bob opens both doors of his placed Room by the special action before his own Leech is on the battlefield (cast after, a creature entering, so its enchantment arm is silent), and alice's Leech does not fire on bob's full unlock (CR 709.5i's \"you\"): every life total is 20 when the lock comes. Roaring Furnace's trigger deals 1, the card in bob's hand, to alice's 2/2 Leech, which survives.",
